# Example: remote Terraform state in S3, for a TEAM (not used by this project).
#
# Why it is not enabled here: the S3 bucket must exist BEFORE Terraform runs, so
# it cannot be created by this same configuration. It would be an extra,
# manually created AWS resource that outlives "terraform destroy" (the opposite
# of what this simulator wants), and this project is a single-user, short-lived
# lab. Local state is a deliberate choice, see "Design Decisions" in the README.
#
# To use it in a team:
#   1. Create a private, versioned, encrypted S3 bucket (outside this project).
#   2. Copy this file to terraform/backend.tf and fill in the bucket name.
#   3. Run: terraform init -migrate-state
#
# State locking stops two people from applying at the same time:
#   - Terraform 1.10 or newer: use_lockfile = true (locks inside the bucket).
#   - Older versions: a DynamoDB table with a "LockID" string key and
#     dynamodb_table = "<table name>".
#
# terraform {
#   backend "s3" {
#     bucket       = "<your-private-state-bucket>"
#     key          = "eks-incident-simulator/terraform.tfstate"
#     region       = "us-east-1"
#     encrypt      = true
#     use_lockfile = true
#   }
# }
